From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:30:48 +0200
Subject: [parser] Preserve strict parameter errors when reparsing lazy arrow
 functions

When a lazy top-level arrow function fails `SkipFunction` due to an
unidentifiable error in its body, `ParseArrowFunctionLiteral` rewinds to
the arrow head and reparses it via `ParseConditionalExpression()`.

Previously, this fallback path did not restore `start_position` on the
reparsed `function_scope` or copy the strict parameter error from
`next_arrow_function_info_` to `parameters`. As a result, cases like
`let f = (eval) => { "use strict"; let x; let x; };` reported the later
body error instead of `Unexpected eval or arguments in strict mode`.

Propagate `start_position` and `strict_parameter_error` to the reparsed
scope and `FormalParametersT`.

